    "raw_text": "Bashline to Host ‘Coffee and Conversation’ May 27\nMay 14, 2026\nHARRISBURG\n– To hear from constituents about issues plaguing the region and Commonwealth, Rep. Josh Bashline (R-Clarion/Armstrong) announced he will be hosting a “coffee and conversation” event on Wednesday, May 27, from 11:30 a.m. to 12:30 p.m., at Ispirare Coffee, located at\n140 Market St. in Kittanning\n.\n“The only way I can best represent the 63rd District is hearing directly from constituents about the issues important to them,” said Bashline. “This is a great opportunity for attendees to hear from me about legislative action in Harrisburg and voice any questions, concerns and ideas they may have. The more we can exchange civil, healthy dialogue, the better off we will be.”\nRegistration is not required. Constituents with questions are asked to call Bashline’s Kittanning district office at 724-954-3613.\nRepresentative Josh Bashline\n63rd Legislative District\nPennsylvania House of Representatives\nMedia Contact: Nate Temple\n717-260-6396\nntemple@pahousegop.com\nShare\nSign Up to Receive Legislative Email Updates\nKeep up-to-date on the latest legislative and community news. Your email address will be used strictly for legislative purposes.\nEmail*\nZIP Code\nSubscribe",
