  {
    "title": "Efforts Continue to Link Residents with Unclaimed Property, Local Entities with Grants, Says Bashline",
    "url": "https://repbashline.com/News/37245/Press-Releases/Efforts-Continue-to-Link-Residents-with-Unclaimed-Property--Local-Entities-with-Grants--Says-Bashline",
    "date": null,
    "raw_text": "Efforts Continue to Link Residents with Unclaimed Property, Local Entities with Grants, Says Bashline\nMarch 3, 2026\nHARRISBURG\n–Rep. Josh Bashline (R-Clarion/Armstrong) announced he will be hosting two events aimed at helping residents and entities within the 63rd District.\nThe first event he will host is his Unclaimed Property “Pot of Gold” event scheduled for Wednesday, March 18, from 11 a.m. to 1 p.m., at the Sugarcreek Township Volunteer Fire Department Hall, located at\n110 Rodgers Road, East Brady\n.\nIn 2025, Bashline’s district office staff, in conjunction with the Pennsylvania Treasurer’s Office, helped residents reclaim $12,221 worth of property. The partnership will continue this year. Separately, his staff will also assist residents with their Property Tax/Rent Rebate applications.\nThe second event is a grant seminar in collaboration with the Pennsylvania Department of Community and Economic Development (DCED). That is scheduled for Friday, March 20, from 11 a.m. to 1 p.m., at the Distant Fire Department Hall, located at 2239 Madison Road, New Bethlehem. Representatives from DCED will be in attendance to provide a presentation on the types of grants available, eligibility requirements and application processes. Township officials, fire departments and nonprofit organizations are encouraged to attend.\n“Constituent services are such an important aspect of my job,” said Bashline. “My dedicated team and I are beyond honored to assist with state-related matters like these.”\nAnyone with questions is asked to call Bashline’s Clarion district office at 814-226-9000 or his Kittanning district office at 724-954-3613.\nRepresentative Josh Bashline\n63rd Legislative District\nPennsylvania House of Representatives\nMedia Contact: Nate Temple\n717-260-6396\nntemple@pahousegop.com\nShare\nSign Up to Receive Legislative Email Updates\nKeep up-to-date on the latest legislative and community news. Your email address will be used strictly for legislative purposes.\nEmail*\nZIP Code\nSubscribe",
    "ai_summary": {
      "summary": "Rep. Josh Bashline is hosting two community events in March 2026: a March 18 event where staff will help residents search for and claim unclaimed property through the Pennsylvania Treasurer's Office, and a March 20 grant seminar where state DCED representatives will explain available grants to local governments, fire departments, and nonprofits. His office also assisted residents in reclaiming over $12,000 in unclaimed property in 2025.",
      "action_type": "event",
      "topics": [
        "economy",
        "other"
      ],
      "spin_flag": true
    }
