  {
    "title": "Fire, EMS Grants Awarded to 63rd District",
    "url": "https://repbashline.com/News/37530/Press-Releases/Fire--EMS-Grants-Awarded-to-63rd-District",
    "date": null,
    "raw_text": "Fire, EMS Grants Awarded to 63rd District\nFebruary 12, 2026\nHARRISBURG\n–Rep. Josh Bashline (R-Clarion/Armstrong) announced more than $460,000 in grant funding will support fire companies and emergency medical services in the 63rd District.\n“Our fire and EMS personnel put service above self every day, answering the call in moments of crisis with professionalism, courage and compassion,” said Bashline. “Their dedication and sacrifice are the backbone of our communities, and we are deeply grateful for all they do to keep us safe. While I appreciate seeing these funds coming to our district, it is not enough. I hope to see heavy increases in future allocations.”\nEstablished by the Legislature, the Fire Company and Emergency Medical Services Grant Program is administered by the Pennsylvania Emergency Management Agency and Office of the State Fire Commissioner. The grant money comes from state gaming proceeds as required under state law. It was first initiated in 2000 and is open to volunteer and career fire companies, emergency medical services and rescue squads in Pennsylvania. Grant awards can be used for construction or repair of facilities, purchase or repair of equipment, debt reduction, recruitment, retention, public education about fire safety and training. The funding amounts are contingent on the recipients filing their grant agreements with the Office of the State Fire Commissioner.\nRecipient companies in the 63rd District include:\nArmstrong County\n•\nDayton District Volunteer Fire Company: $13,044.82.\n•\nDistant Area Volunteer Fire Department: $12,632.59.\n•\nElderton District Volunteer Fire Company: $12,014.25.\n•\nHose Company No. 6 Kittanning (EMS): $15,000.\n•\nHose Company No. 6 Kittanning (Fire): $13,457.05.\n•\nHose Hook and Ladder Company No. 1 Inc.: $12,220.36.\n•\nKittanning Hose Company No. 4: $12,220.36.\n•\nKittanning Township Volunteer Fire Department No. 1: $13,044.82.\n•\nParker City Volunteer Fire Company: $25,457.05.\n•\nPine Township Volunteer Fire Company: $12,838.71.\n•\nRayburn Township Volunteer Fire Company: $11,679.\n•\nRural Valley Hose Company: $12,220.36\n•\nSugarcreek Township Volunteer Fire Department: $13,869.28.\n•\nWashington Township Volunteer Fire Department: $12,014.25.\n•\nWorthington West Franklin Volunteer Fire Department: $12,014.25.\nClarion County\n•\nCallensburg-Licking Township Volunteer Fire Company: $12,426.48.\n•\nClarion Fire and Hose Company No. 1: $12,220.36.\n•\nClarion Hospital: $15,000.\n•\nEast Brady Area Ambulance Service: $15,000.\n•\nEast Brady Volunteer Fire Department: $13,457.05.\n•\nFarmington Township Volunteer Fire Company: $12,014.25.\n•\nHawthorn Area Volunteer Fire Department: $12,014.25.\n•\nKnox Area Volunteer Ambulance Company Inc.: $15,000.\n•\nKnox Volunteer Fire Company: $13,250.94.\n•\nLimestone Township Volunteer Fire Company: $12,014.25.\n•\nMill Creek Township Volunteer Fire Department: $12,014.25.\n•\nNew Bethlehem Fire Company No. 1: $12,632.59.\n•\nPerry Township Volunteer Fire Department: $12,014.25.\n•\nRimersburg Hose Company: $12,220.36.\n•\nShippenville Elk Township Volunteer Fire Department: $12,220.36.\n•\nSligo Volunteer Fire Department Inc.: $12,220.36.\n•\nSouthern Clarion County Volunteer Ambulance: $15,000.\n•\nSt. Petersburg Volunteer Fire Company: $12,014.25.\n•\nStrattanville Volunteer Fire Department: $12,220.36.\n•\nWashington Township Volunteer Fire Department: $12,220.36.\nRepresentative Josh Bashline\n63rd Legislative District\nPennsylvania House of Representatives\nMedia Contact: Nate Temple\n717-260-6396\nntemple@pahousegop.com\nShare\nSign Up to Receive Legislative Email Updates\nKeep up-to-date on the latest legislative and community news. Your email address will be used strictly for legislative purposes.\nEmail*\nZIP Code\nSubscribe",
    "ai_summary": {
      "summary": "The Pennsylvania Emergency Management Agency and Office of the State Fire Commissioner awarded over $460,000 in state grants to 35 fire companies and EMS organizations across Armstrong and Clarion counties in the 63rd District. The grants come from a long-standing state program funded by gaming proceeds and can be used for equipment, facilities, training, and recruitment. Rep. Bashline announced the awards and called for larger allocations in the future.",
      "action_type": "award",
      "topics": [
        "public_safety"
      ],
      "spin_flag": true
    }
